/target/
/.claude/
# Per-platform libneedle engine binaries (feature `ffi`). Apache-2.0 and
# redistributable, but a 1.1 MB blob per target that `cargo check`/`just
# verify` never need — fetch on demand, see crates/needle-sys/build.rs.
# `crates/needle-sys/needle.h` (the API contract) IS committed.
/crates/needle-sys/vendor/
.cursorindexingignore
.specstory/
specs/scratch.md

# Per-project forge state: config.toml, the built graph, session transcripts.
# Unanchored so nested projects are covered too, not just the repo root.
.forge/

# Local secrets, and anything an editor or tool leaves beside them
# (`.env.backup`, `.env.local`, `.env.save`, …). `.env` was previously covered
# only by individual developers' global gitignore, which a fresh clone cannot
# rely on — so one careless `git add -A` could have committed real credentials.
# The example file lives at examples/env.example and is unaffected by these
# patterns; the negations guard against a dotfile variant being added later.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
!.env.sample
